is about um about  cordiality  and  usually you receive more than  than  than  you give if you're a cordial so we will  certainly get uh  everything that we need for for covering  our needs we are all uh as one in this  so  the money will not be your problem at  the european  union so  what we're talking about even about  about 100 coverage but as i said this is  not a matter of the money it's a matter  of being human  very noble answer  rest assure that the european solidarity  of course  is there to support a country like  slovakia in what you're doing now  you have enormous expenses  the staff that is working you need to  give food water shelter to the refugees  and of course we stand up together as  europeans from the european budget  to support slovakia in that  the biggest gift you are giving is the  human warmth and the reception of the  refugees this is priceless if i may say  so  on your second question if i got it  right whether slovakia will benefit from  the gas solidarity of course  i mean we have in the last years  invested heavily in lng terminals that's  good  because that helps us now we have from  all over the world starting with the  united states but other suppliers egypt  for example are also who want to step up  their lng  supplies to the european union we have  more than 25 lng terminals  to get the resources and thanks to a  massive investment over the last years  in pipelines and interconnectors  we have a pipeline network all over the  european union  that enables us to basically send the  gas to where it is needed  and therefore of course  slovakia will be supported if need be  on top we still have the storage  slovakia also has quite substantial  storage and this combination makes it  for us possible  to in case of decoupling of russian gas  to make it  now throughout the winter with the own  supplies that we are able to get  bloomberg  any other question of bloomberg  from bloomberg i would like to ask the  president uh  how the the european commission will  respond uh to uh the application for  becoming a member of the european union  from the side of ukraine so now what  should be the response and then now we  see that also moldavia and  georgia  show their interest as well  i think it is very important  first of all to say  that these brave people in ukraine  that are willing to fight for our common  universal values  and to die for our universal values  belong in our european family without  any doubt  now indeed president zelinski has sent a  letter on ukraine's application  and indeed there is  the  moldova  and georgian wish also to send a letter  concerning an application  and by that  president celensky has set a process  in motion  and this process is now evolving  it will be the next step that the  leaders the member states will discuss  that  but there is a process ongoing and this  is a positive development  um we have before the war already had  special outstanding relationship with  ukraine  i always emphasize that we have started  to integrate the different  markets  strong economic ties  we have been working intensively on  energy security for ukraine that pays  off now in these days  we have the deep and comprehensive free  trade agreement  with ukraine so a lot of steps have  already been done in the days before the  war  now with this application a process is  put in motion  and it  will be discussed in the appropriate  different settings  what i can add to that was that uh is  that slovakia was one of the first  country uh that  supported ukraine in their ambition to  become a member of the eu and it's only  natural we are their neighbor we  understand them  and our mutual relations uh uh are got  uh  very intensive i would like to share a  story you know that that we heard on  uh on a thursday uh from a former uh  prime minister  uh  and uh uh who who oh it was a prime  prime minister of slovenia um  and uh he said that  when they set their application back in  the 90s and  and  that it was a very important moment for  them when they received a a promise or a  positive motion so uh i believe that it  is equally important to send the signal  to ukraine as well and  dr president uh was very clear in saying  that they are part of our  european family and the many members of  the european uh union share  this vision and this uh this reflects  how we see our ukrainian friends the  last thing that i would like to say to  that is that  last thursday we  we woke up to a new world and that is  why we have to look for new ways we have  to come up with new rules so that we  allow country that is in a very unique  situation unlike any other country that  are that have the ambition there to  become a member of the eu this country  is tried by war is devastated by war and  will be devastated  by by the war  let's hope that they will they will keep  their independence they will keep their  government um but  unfortunately if the when the war is  over they will be devastated  so we will  we will need to help them and support  them to get back on their feet as soon  as possible  and this new way of thinking uh i think  this will be reflected in our mutual  communications and negotiations and we  will find ways how to bring them to to  our family as soon as possible thank you  and this is moldova and georgia i just  want to be very clear that they have our  unwavering support too  and moldova you were mentioning moldova  is hosting also many many refugees  therefore  help and support from the european union  is guaranteed in kind but also  financially it's outstanding what  moldova is doing at the moment being  taking in refugees from their neighbor  ukraine and of course we support them in  dealing with that situation but also  to make it possible for the refugees to  move on to the european union  thank you and have a nice day
 

